The temperature measurement system was organised at different points uniformly distributed at suitable distances from both sides of the fire source. The measurement positions were chosen to follow a log-Tchebychev distribution of grid points, so that the average temperature was equal to the arithmetic mean of the measured values. The same scheme was adopted for velocity measurements.
